.TH COBOLLM 1 "September 2026" "COBOLLM" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cobollm \- run a small unsandboxed coding agent written in COBOL
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SS GNU/Linux
.B cobollm
.I TASK
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cobollm
sends one task to an OpenAI-compatible Responses endpoint.
The model can call one custom tool named
.BR shell .
Each tool call starts a fresh
.B /bin/sh
in the current directory.
Shell-local state does not survive between calls, but filesystem changes do.
.PP
The shell runs with the COBOLLM process user's permissions.
COBOLLM has no sandbox, permission check, confirmation prompt, or command
timeout.
Model-supplied commands can read, change, and delete any data available to that
user.
.PP
COBOLLM keeps one session in process memory.
It sends accepted Responses output items and shell results back on later turns
with
.BR store:false .
It does not stream, save sessions, or resume a prior session.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I TASK
Exactly one nonempty GNU/Linux command-line argument.
The maximum length is 65,535 bytes.
.SH INPUT
.TP
.B TASK DD
On z/OS, a protected USS regular byte file containing 1 through 65,535 native
IBM-1047 bytes.
Spaces, newlines, and trailing bytes are preserved.
A 65,536th byte is rejected.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPENAI_API_KEY
Required bearer token, limited to 8,192 printable ASCII bytes without spaces.
COBOLLM removes this variable from the child environment before running a
shell command.
The key remains in parent process memory until cleanup, and a same-user command
may be able to inspect that process.
.TP
.B OPENAI_MODEL
Required model identifier, limited to 256 bytes.
.B gpt-5.3-codex
is an example.
Its availability depends on the endpoint and account.
.TP
.B OPENAI_BASE_URL
Optional Responses base URL, limited to 2,048 bytes.
The default is
.BR https://api.openai.com/v1 .
COBOLLM strips trailing path slashes and appends
.BR /responses .
.PP
The z/OS run JCL reads these values from a protected
.B RUNENV
data set allocated with RECFM=V and LRECL 8211 or larger.
Each record contains one native IBM-1047
.B NAME=value
entry.
CEEOPTS forces
.B _BPXK_AUTOCVT=OFF
outside RUNENV to preserve the native task bytes.
.SH ENDPOINT
The URL parser accepts an HTTP or HTTPS URL with an ASCII DNS hostname,
optional port, and optional origin path.
It rejects IP literals, user information, query strings, fragments,
backslashes, whitespace, non-ASCII bytes, and invalid DNS labels.
.PP
GNU HTTPS uses OpenSSL 3 default trust paths, SNI, certificate-chain
verification, and hostname verification.
GNU plain HTTP is permitted with a warning.
The z/OS target rejects plain HTTP.
Before writing HTTP, it requires AT-TLS to report policy enabled, connection
secure, security type client, and an allowed protocol and cipher.
Policy provenance is a separate mandatory deployment gate.
.SH RESPONSES PROTOCOL
Each request sets
.BR store:false ,
.BR parallel_tool_calls:false ,
and requests
.BR reasoning.encrypted_content .
It advertises one custom free-form tool named
.BR shell .
.PP
COBOLLM accepts reasoning items, custom shell calls, and completed assistant
messages from the endpoint.
It rejects parallel calls and unsupported output shapes.
.SH LIMITS
.TP
Shell command
65,535 bytes.
.TP
Shell output
1 MiB after UTF-8 conversion.
.TP
Final response
1 MiB of UTF-8.
.TP
HTTP response body
8 MiB.
.TP
Conversation history and request body
16 MiB each.
.TP
HTTP response headers
64 KiB.
.TP
JSON nesting
64 levels.
.SH OUTPUT
COBOLLM writes shell activity and diagnostics to standard error.
It merges shell standard error into shell standard output and returns both to
the model.
The final model response goes to standard output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The model returned a final response and COBOLLM wrote it successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Internal invariant or output failure.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or configuration failure.
.TP
.B 3
HTTP, JSON, or Responses protocol failure.
.TP
.B 4
Network or TLS failure.
.TP
.B 5
Shell runtime failure.
.TP
.B 6
Fixed capacity or text-conversion failure.
.SH SECURITY
Run COBOLLM only inside an environment that can tolerate arbitrary commands
from the configured endpoint.
Removing
.B OPENAI_API_KEY
from the shell environment does not isolate the parent process or protect other
same-user credentials and files.
.SH PLATFORM STATUS
The GNU build supports one checked Linux/aarch64 ABI family.
The z/OS build JCL is configured to compile RENT objects and bind one MVS
program object with
.BR REUS(NONE) .
Separate run JCL is configured to launch it directly from MVS batch with
.BR POSIX(ON) .
Nobody has compiled, bound, or run these artifacts on z/OS.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sh (1)
